1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,218
This is STE-80. It is a writing style for technical text.

2
00:00:04,318 --> 00:00:09,907
It comes from ASD-STE100, Simplified Technical English, a standard for

3
00:00:10,007 --> 00:00:12,312
aircraft maintenance manuals.

4
00:00:12,412 --> 00:00:16,229
The eighty means about eighty percent of the way to strict STE:

5
00:00:16,329 --> 00:00:20,086
it keeps the writing rules and drops the approved dictionary.

6
00:00:20,186 --> 00:00:24,142
Manuals are read under time pressure, often in a second language, so

7
00:00:24,242 --> 00:00:25,376
every word must help.

8
00:00:26,476 --> 00:00:30,399
Here is a typical sentence from a manual. It has sixteen words:

9
00:00:30,499 --> 00:00:34,052
the orange bar counts them. Some of the words do not help the reader.

10
00:00:34,143 --> 00:00:38,754
Rule one. Use simple words: the common word, not the formal one.

11
00:00:38,854 --> 00:00:42,377
The words in red change. Replenished becomes full.

12
00:00:42,477 --> 00:00:46,106
Prior to becomes before. Commencing becomes starting.

13
00:00:46,206 --> 00:00:49,370
Only one word goes, but each word is easier to read.

14
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:54,120
Rule two. Give the instruction directly.

15
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:57,499
Cut the opening that only says the instruction matters.

16
00:00:57,599 --> 00:01:01,263
Tell the reader what to do instead: make sure, before you start.

17
00:01:01,363 --> 00:01:02,372
Thirteen words.

18
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:05,757
Rule three. Use concrete words.

19
00:01:05,857 --> 00:01:09,337
The phrase make sure that it is full asks the reader to check a

20
00:01:09,437 --> 00:01:09,841
result.

21
00:01:09,941 --> 00:01:13,881
The verb fill names the action, and the machine names what you start.

22
00:01:13,981 --> 00:01:14,927
Nine words.

23
00:01:16,527 --> 00:01:18,441
Sixteen words became nine.

24
00:01:18,541 --> 00:01:22,063
The reader still fills the reservoir before starting the machine, with

25
00:01:22,163 --> 00:01:23,134
less work to read it.

26
00:01:24,227 --> 00:01:27,105
The bar counts words, but the goal is less work:

27
00:01:27,205 --> 00:01:29,780
rule one cut only one word and still helped.

28
00:01:30,377 --> 00:01:32,892
STE-80 has more rules than these three:

29
00:01:32,992 --> 00:01:36,357
short sentences, one meaning per word, and no filler.
